{"title":"Career Roadmap — Pharma QA Executive","role":"Pharma QA Executive","summary":"A Pharma QA (Quality Assurance) Executive ensures that pharmaceutical products, manufacturing processes, laboratories, documentation, and quality systems comply with established GMP, quality, safety, and regulatory requirements.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science - General / Honours)","Course":"Microbiology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Pharma QA (Quality Assurance) Executive ensures that pharmaceutical products, manufacturing processes, laboratories, documentation, and quality systems comply with established GMP, quality, safety, and regulatory requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Microbiology graduate, this is a strong pathway because microbiology directly supports sterility assurance, environmental monitoring, microbial contamination control, water-system monitoring, aseptic manufacturing, and microbiological quality systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical sectors include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmaceutical manufacturing"},{"text":"Biopharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Vaccines"},{"text":"Sterile/injectable manufacturing"},{"text":"Medical products"},{"text":"Contract manufacturing"},{"text":"Quality-control laboratories"},{"text":"Clinical and research organizations"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"B.Sc Microbiology can support entry-level QA/QC opportunities, but progression into higher-level QA, compliance, validation, or managerial positions is often strengthened by relevant postgraduate education and practical GMP experience."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc Microbiology"},{"text":"Microbiology + GMP + QA fundamentals + laboratory exposure"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"QA Trainee / Junior QA 